{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1696,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The story goes, this man's candy bar melted in his pocket, and nothing in the room was hot.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 129
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "His name was Percy Spencer. He never finished grammar school, and taught himself the science from books.",
   "from": 133,
   "to": 292
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In the war he worked on radar tubes called magnetrons. His method made two thousand six hundred a day.",
   "from": 296,
   "to": 436
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But standing next to a running magnetron, he found sticky chocolate all over his pocket.",
   "from": 439,
   "to": 558
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He grabbed raw popcorn kernels and held them by the tube. They popped all over the lab.",
   "from": 561,
   "to": 673
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Next, an egg in a kettle. It shook, and then it burst.",
   "from": 676,
   "to": 767
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "colleague",
   "text": "Percy, look out!",
   "from": 771,
   "to": 794
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So how does a radar tube cook without any fire?",
   "from": 798,
   "to": 871
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, the tube sends out microwaves. They make the water inside food twist back and forth.",
   "from": 886,
   "to": 1016
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "All that rubbing between molecules turns into heat, right inside the food. No flame at all.",
   "from": 1020,
   "to": 1144
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "On October eighth, nineteen forty-five, a patent was filed for cooking with microwaves.",
   "from": 1148,
   "to": 1259
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The first oven, in nineteen forty-seven, stood six feet tall and weighed seven hundred and fifty pounds.",
   "from": 1262,
   "to": 1392
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Twenty years later, in nineteen sixty-seven, a countertop model cost four hundred ninety-five dollars.",
   "from": 1395,
   "to": 1539
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So every bag of microwave popcorn goes back to one melted candy bar.",
   "from": 1542,
   "to": 1672
  }
 ],
